<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Your data, plainly explained"
  description="ilyStream is designed as a local-first broadcast studio. This policy explains what the app processes, when information leaves your computer, and the choices you control."
  updated="July 12, 2026"
>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    ilyStream is a Windows desktop application for composing, managing, recording, and publishing
    livestreams. Most application settings, scenes, event history, audience statistics, logs, and
    credentials are stored on your computer. ilyStream does not sell personal information or use it
    for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Information ilyStream processes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information.</strong> When you connect a streaming or media platform, ilyStream may process account identifiers, display names, avatars, channel information, and authorization status.</li>
    <li><strong>Livestream activity.</strong> The app may process chat messages, usernames, gifts, follows, likes, viewer counts, moderation status, and other events exposed by the platforms you connect.</li>
    <li><strong>Broadcast media.</strong> Camera, microphone, screen, application-window, and mixed program output are processed to preview, record, or publish the broadcast you configure.</li>
    <li><strong>Local configuration and diagnostics.</strong> Scenes, source settings, automations, widget configuration, application logs, and crash details generated by the app may be stored locally to make the product work and help diagnose problems.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When information leaves your computer</h2>
  <p>
    ilyStream sends information to a third party only when necessary for a feature you choose. For
    example, starting a broadcast sends encoded audio and video to the selected streaming platform;
    connecting an account sends authorization requests to that platform; and using a cloud service
    sends the content required for that service to respond.
  </p>
  <p>
    Depending on your setup, those services may include TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, Kick, Spotify, X,
    Philips Hue, Govee, update hosting, and other destinations you explicitly configure. Their own
    privacy policies govern how they process information after receiving it.
  </p>

  <h2>TikTok authorization and LIVE access</h2>
  <p>
    If official TikTok Login Kit or native TikTok LIVE publishing is enabled, TikTok displays the
    requested permissions before you authorize ilyStream. TikTok client secrets, refresh tokens, and
    partner-only LIVE API calls are handled by an HTTPS authorization service rather than being
    embedded in the desktop application. The desktop app stores only the minimum encrypted session
    credential needed to use that service. Disconnecting the official account invalidates that
    session and requests deletion or revocation of the related server-side credentials.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
  <p>
    Local application data is generally stored under the ilyStream application-data directory on
    your Windows account. You control that data and may remove it by resetting the relevant feature,
    disconnecting accounts, or uninstalling the app and deleting its application-data folder.
    Server-side authorization records, when applicable, are retained only while needed to keep the
    connection active, meet security obligations, or comply with law.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    ilyStream uses operating-system encryption for supported credentials, limits renderer access to
    approved desktop operations, and avoids placing service secrets in public source code. No system
    can guarantee absolute security, so users should keep Windows, ilyStream, and connected accounts
    updated and protected.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    ilyStream is not directed to children. Users must satisfy the age, account, and LIVE eligibility
    requirements of every platform they connect.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
  <p>
    You can decline platform permissions, disconnect accounts, stop a broadcast, and delete local
    application data. For help with a privacy request, visit the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}support/`}>support page</a>.
    Do not post passwords, API keys, tokens, cookies, or other sensitive information in a public issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Policy changes</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may be updated as ilyStream adds integrations or changes how information is
    processed. The date above identifies the latest revision.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
